  "method": "Original TWD97 source geometry; exact original endpoints form nodes; interiors stay per source part. Checks run in order road/crossing, OSM blocker or active construction, then complete official pedestrian area union with the stated buffer. OSM pedestrian edges were prefiltered with production edgeAllowed and explicit grade/bridge/tunnel exclusions. Distance and polygon operations in EPSG:3826. Attachment to OSM is counted per exact source graph component; this is a geometric opportunity, not a route success count. Sample source segments are the first eligible examples by source order, not statistically representative.",
  "limitations": "Buffered area and nearby-endpoint links are estimated, not confirmed sidewalk alignment or connectivity. Original official line contains no elevation, layer or pedestrian access attributes; even zero tolerance and exact endpoint equality do not establish same-level passage. Road centreline intersection evidence and construction records can be incomplete. OSM shared-road edges excluded from attachment analysis. Construction is one time-limited snapshot; all route results require fresh revalidation. No user-selected points, real journey outcomes, or production graph writes are included."
